commits.message:
[skyrl] Delete critic training, FlashQLA and unused SkyRL helpers (#10660)

Vendored SkyRL supports only critic-free training and the PyTorch GatedDeltaNet path, and code that nothing calls is deleted. No config, nightly test or launcher on `main` selects a critic or `generator.gdn_backend=flashqla`, so existing runs behave the same.

Deleted code:

- critic (value model) training: GAE advantages, the critic worker classes, the critic loss and normalization, the value and returns fields of `Experience`, the critic trainer steps, the `trainer.critic` config section, the critic placement keys and `trainer.critic_mini_batch_size`, and the checks of `trainer.critic.model.path` in validation, FTPO, DPO, the marin launcher and checkpoint export;
- the FlashQLA GatedDeltaNet kernel, its `generator.gdn_backend` setting and the TileLang cache sync the Iris launcher ran around it;
- the no-op telemetry fallback used when `rigging` is not installed;
- in the vLLM actor, the unused accumulate-then-load weight update with its FP8 requantization, the uncalled FP8 weight-loader patch, and the expert-slot readers;
- the MoE router instrumentation and its Grug emitter, and the Grug optimizer route snapshot;
- the `generate/tis/lcs_fallback_fraction`, `lcs_fallback_messages` and `lcs_fallback_alert` metrics, which rollout finalization sets to 0 for every row; the alignment alert reads unaligned tokens and TITO declines;
- the deferred worker checkpoint upload and the trainer's wait on it; no worker produces an upload;
- helpers nothing calls, among them the weight-sync tensor helper, the validation-generation logger, search-environment answer scoring, GenRM prompt keys, a NUMA page probe, launcher secrets and model-path helpers, and GPU test utilities the Grug parity tests do not import;
- base-config keys that no production code reads: the policy LoRA settings other than `rank` and `adapter_path`, `use_torch_compile`, the policy optimizer's `offload_after_step`, `trainer.attn_backend`, `tis_splice`, `tis_lcs_alert_threshold`, `lambd`, `value_clip` and `value_head_prefix`, with the matching fields of the typed recipe schema;
- the tests of the code above, and tests of remaining code that repeat another test or only check that a config field is passed through. Some launcher config tests are combined into fewer tests that check the same behavior, and the FlashAttention context-parallel test gains an entropy-loss-only case.

Settings:

- Training is critic-free. A source recipe that sets any `trainer.critic` key fails at launch with an unknown-key error. The advantage estimators are GRPO, RLOO, RLOO-N, RLOO-N-PBS, REINFORCE++, uniform and reward. The `train_critic_and_policy` timing key keeps its name, so dashboards read the same field.
- GatedDeltaNet layers run the PyTorch path, as on `main`. The Iris launcher starts the controller with `exec` for every config.
- Telemetry requires the `rigging` package.
- A source recipe that sets any other key in the deletion list fails at launch with an unknown-key error. A launch config that already holds a composed SkyRL section, such as an earlier run's resolved config, loads and ignores those keys.

One runtime difference: the GPU count that decides whether NCCL peer-to-peer and shared-memory transport stay enabled is the largest of the policy GPUs per node, the reference GPUs per node and the inference tensor-parallel size. It changes only for runs where all three are 1: those runs skip the peer-access probe and disable NCCL peer-to-peer and shared-memory transport.

`build_models` takes the policy and reference worker classes, and `get_worker_classes` returns those two.

The results below compare head 5ae897fe00 with `main` at dbac7175df. Later merges of `main` bring in its own changes, including worker batch assembly (#10668), with no deleted name reintroduced; CI passes on the current head. On CPU, the unit tests and the 13 nightly cases pass; the `main` run passes the same tests except the CatCount resume nightly case, which is intermittent on `main` and failed in that run. The 393 remaining modules import with the same results as on `main`; the six deleted modules are the only difference. The 215 launcher config combinations give the same result as on `main`: 206 build byte-identical configs and 9 fail the same geometry check. On H100, with each Grug MoE test run in its own clean attention-backend environment, all 52 tests that `main` runs pass on both trees, the added entropy-loss case passes, and the 88 numerical parity values the tests print equal `main`'s. The CatCount RL smoke run completes 10 steps and passes all of its checks, and its sampled training score at step 10 (0.690) is inside the range of repeated `main` runs (0.64 to 0.71).
